MerkleAdapterLiquidity
├── when liquid cash is present
│   ├── it stays investable until requested, staged or released
│   ├── it becomes withdrawable only after a covering report releases it
│   ├── released withdrawals cannot exceed cash or accounted portfolio NAV
│   └── completed payments decrement demand and capital flow
├── when liquidity is requested
│   ├── it protects available cash from reinvestment
│   ├── it keeps unfunded demand without freezing valid reports
│   ├── it records all new allocations without refunding unreported cash
│   ├── later arrivals keep the first staged batch and wait for another report
│   ├── cancelling demand preserves already staged and released cash
│   └── outgoing cash cannot be staged again before the delegator transfers it
└── when the oracle is frozen
    ├── raw liquidity remains observable without oracle validation
    └── the delegator final validation rolls back cash, demand and checkpoints atomically
